  "text": "Bring the short ends of the bridge sections together. Turn the loose section to face the same way as the other section.\n\nPip asked Grandma about starting later. She agreed. Invitations and the reader still depend on the actual chosen plan.\n\nHere, stones hold the cloth in place. At the river, fastenings hold the crossing in place. The wind was still blowing.\n\nTry my ending lets you look at it first. Use this ending selects those exact words. Back takes you to where you were.\n\nChoose a memory in Grandma’s conversation, then place it in Pip’s flower. Afterward, finish the closing conversation.\n\nWrite what Pip will tell Grandma about Mara’s work and when she could come. You are preparing a message for Grandma.\n\nMara says: “Please ask Grandma. A later gathering would give me time to finish work. The time has not changed yet.”\n\nTo carry the seed instead, steer back to the yellow launch and unload it. Help and Pause keep the boat where it is.\n\nThe SparkFest group together: four children, Loop the rolling projector, and the paper characters Pip and Grandma.\n\nAn earlier service today: the operator brings the boat in. Mara helps these passengers ashore, then stays on duty.\n\nThe boy holds the repaired original bird in both hands. “Now I can tell my grandmother how we fixed it,” he says.\n\nHelp and Pause stop Mara’s travel. A tape preview is canceled; an already placed strip stays where you placed it.\n\nRina says: “Yes. You may take the spare tile from that shelf. Bring it to Sol so he can replace the cracked one.”\n\nPip helped divide the dough. Rina shaped the pieces into three loaves and arranged them with space between them.\n\nThe complete telling plays in order. Pause or replay whenever you like, or open the full text with reading help.",
